     *   quickly", "inject emotion into your voice", "laugh frequently"). The instructions are not
     *   guaranteed to be followed by the model, but they provide…
     * @param voice The voice the model uses to respond. Supported built-in voices are `alloy`,
     *   `ash`, `ballad`, `coral`, `echo`, `sage`, `shimmer`, `verse`, `marin`, and `cedar`. You may
     *   also provide a custom voice object with an `id`, for example `{ "id": "voice_1234" }`.
     *   Voice cannot be changed during the session once the model has responded with audio at least
     *   once. Custom voices must be created from audio samples.
     * @param inputAudioFormat The format of input audio. Options are `pcm16`, `g711_ulaw`, or
     *   `g711_alaw`.
     * @param outputAudioFormat The format of output audio. Options are `pcm16`, `g711_ulaw`, or
     *   `g711_alaw`.
     * @param inputAudioTranscription Configuration for input audio transcription, defaults to off
     *   and can be set to `null` to turn off once on. Input audio transcription is not native to
     *   the model, since the model consumes audio directly. Transcription runs asynchronously and
     *   should be treated as rough guidance rather than the representation understood by the model.
     * @param speed The speed of the model's spoken response. 1.0 is the default speed. 0.25 is the
     *   minimum speed. 1.5 is the maximum speed. This value can only be changed in between model
     *   turns, not while a response is in progress.
     * @param tracing Configuration options for tracing. Set to null to disable tracing. Once
     *   tracing is enabled for a session, the configuration cannot be modified. `auto` will create
     *   a trace for the session with default values for the workflow name, group id, and metadata.
     * @param turnDetection Configuration for turn detection. Can be set to `null` to turn off.
     *   Server VAD means that the model will detect the start and end of speech based on audio
     *   volume and respond at the end of user speech.
     * @param tools Tools (functions) available to the model.
     * @param toolChoice How the model chooses tools. Options are `auto`, `none`, `required`, or
     *   specify a function.
     * @param temperature Sampling temperature for the model, limited to \[0.6, 1.2\]. Defaults to
     *   0.8.
     * @param maxResponseOutputTokens Maximum number of output tokens for a single assistant
     *   response, inclusive of tool calls. Provide an integer between 1 and 4096 to limit output
     *   tokens, or `inf` for the maximum available tokens for a given model. Defaults to `inf`.
     * @param truncation When the number of tokens in a conversation exceeds the model's input token
     *   limit, the conversation be truncated, meaning messages (starting from the oldest) will not
     *   be included in the model's context. A 32k context model with 4,096 max output tokens can
     *   only include 28,224 tokens in the context before truncation occurs. Clients can configure
     *   truncation behavior to truncate with a lower max token limit, which is an effective way to
     *   control token usage and cost. Truncation…
     * @param prompt Reference to a prompt template and its variables. Learn more.
     */
    fun createRealtimeSession(
        clientConfig: ClientConfig,
        request: CreateRealtimeSessionRequest,
        options: RequestOptions? = null,
    ): RealtimeSessionCreateResponse {
        validateCreateRealtimeSessionRequest(request)

        return SdkClient.request<RealtimeSessionCreateResponse>(
                SdkClient.RequestSpec(
                    "POST",
                    "/realtime/sessions",
                    config = clientConfig,
                    body = buildCreateRealtimeSessionBody(request),
                    operationId = "createRealtimeSession",
                    decoder = SdkClient.ResponseDecoder.JSON,
                    options = options,
                )
            )
            .data
    }

    private fun validateCreateRealtimeSessionRequest(request: CreateRealtimeSessionRequest) {
        if (request.speed != null) {
            Validation.validateRange(
                "speed",
                request.speed,
                Validation.RangeOpts(min = 0.25, max = 1.5),
            )
        }
    }

    private fun buildCreateRealtimeSessionBody(
        request: CreateRealtimeSessionRequest
    ): Map<String, Any?> = buildMap {
        putAll(buildCreateRealtimeSessionBodyPart1(request))
        putAll(buildCreateRealtimeSessionBodyPart2(request))
    }

    private fun buildCreateRealtimeSessionBodyPart1(
        request: CreateRealtimeSessionRequest
    ): Map<String, Any?> =
        SdkClient.bodyMap(
            "client_secret" to (request.clientSecret),
            "modalities" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.modalities)),
            "instructions" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.instructions)),
            "voice" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.voice)),
            "input_audio_format" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.inputAudioFormat)),
            "output_audio_format" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.outputAudioFormat)),
            "input_audio_transcription" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.inputAudioTranscription)),
            "speed" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.speed)),
            "tracing" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.tracing)),
            "turn_detection" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.turnDetection)),
            "tools" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.tools)),
            "tool_choice" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.toolChoice)),
        )

    private fun buildCreateRealtimeSessionBodyPart2(
        request: CreateRealtimeSessionRequest
    ): Map<String, Any?> =
        SdkClient.bodyMap(
            "temperature" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.temperature)),
            "max_response_output_tokens" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.maxResponseOutputTokens)),
            "truncation" to (SdkClient.omitIfNull(request.truncation)),
            "prompt" to (request.prompt ?: SdkClient.SdkOptional.Omitted),
        )

    /**
     * Create an ephemeral API token for use in client-side applications with the Realtime API
     * specifically for realtime transcriptions. Can be configured with the same session parameters
     * as the `transcription_session.update` client event. It responds with a session object, plus a
     * `client_secret` key which contains a usable ephemeral API token that can be used to
     * authenticate browser clients for the Realtime API. Returns the created Realtime transcription
     * session object, plus an…
     *
     * @param turnDetection Configuration for turn detection. Can be set to `null` to turn off.
     *   Server VAD means that the model will detect the start and end of speech based on audio
     *   volume and respond at the end of user speech.
     * @param inputAudioNoiseReduction Configuration for input audio noise reduction. This can be
     *   set to `null` to turn off. Noise reduction filters audio added to the input audio buffer
     *   before it is sent to VAD and the model. Filtering the audio can improve VAD and turn
     *   detection accuracy (reducing false positives) and model performance by improving perception
     *   of the input audio.
     * @param inputAudioFormat The format of input audio. Options are `pcm16`, `g711_ulaw`, or
     *   `g711_alaw`. For `pcm16`, input audio must be 16-bit PCM at a 24kHz sample rate, single
     *   channel (mono), and little-endian byte order.
     * @param inputAudioTranscription Configuration for input audio transcription. The client can
     *   optionally set the language and prompt for transcription, these offer additional guidance
